# Chefaa Medications 1401+ Extraction Progress and Evidence-Aligned Update Plan

## Executive Overview and Objectives

The objective is to deliver a robust, evidence-backed pharmaceutical dataset for Chefaa products indexed 1401 and beyond, culminating in a consolidated, clinically credible JSON record set suitable for analytics and operations. This report consolidates what has been reliably extracted so far, identifies and quantifies the remaining gaps, and sets out a pragmatic, evidence-first plan to complete the work within strict step and efficiency constraints.

Progress snapshot. To date, six high-quality product evidence packs have been compiled from Chefaa product pages across antibiotics, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs), diabetes, and antacids. These provide a strong calibration baseline for clinical fields, dosing ranges, pricing anchors, and safety content: Augmentin (amoxicillin/clavulanic acid), Floxamo (amoxicillin/flucloxacillin), Victoza (liraglutide), Sapofen 400 (ibuprofen), Nurofen children’s syrup (ibuprofen), and Duphalac (lactulose).[^4][^5][^6][^7][^8][^11] Evidence for Telfast 180 (fexofenadine) further strengthens the antihistamine class representation.[^10] Together, these cover core therapeutic classes and validate the schema against real-world detail pages.

Narrative arc. First, we define the concrete scope, anchor the 1401+ sequence, and document provenance and extraction constraints. Next, we standardize the data model based on the evidence set and codify validation rules. We then present extracted exemplars and synthesis findings across categories, summarize pricing anchors, and propose a streamlined plan to scale to the remaining products within the step limit. Finally, we define the QA, acceptance criteria, and file output specification. The plan is deliberately evidence-grounded and staged, prioritizing field coverage, clinical reliability, and speed to value.

