### Production Write Plan

- Construct canonical list from page files; deduplicate/normalize per rules; slice 1401+; sort by product_id.
- Serialize to target JSON with metadata.
- Compute and record checksums; maintain a change log with counts, rule versions, and exceptions.

## Risk Register and Mitigation Strategies

Table 8. Risk Register

| Risk | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Missing pages (5,6,7,68) | Coverage gaps | Medium | Gap flagging; alternate link sources; annotate metadata | Data engineering |
| Zero-result pages | Incomplete sequences | Medium | Re-run windows; accept reproducible counts | Data engineering |
| Constructed URL validation | Retrieval failure | Medium | Slug harvesting; multi-locale check; listing corroboration | Data engineering |
| Dynamic content errors | Fetch failures | Medium | Retries/backoff; concurrency caps | Data engineering |
| Partial clinical fields | Sparse safety/indications | High | Staged enrichment; leaflet references; class defaults | Clinical editor |
| Price anomalies | Analytical noise | Medium | Source preference rules; currency tagging; QA flags | Data curation |
| Language/transliteration variants | Mismatched merges | High | Normalization pipeline; alias lists; manual review | Data curation |

These mitigations prioritize throughput and clinical fidelity while acknowledging the operational realities of dynamic, multilingual product pages.[^2][^3]

## Information Gaps

- Active ingredient is not explicitly stated on the Aerius product page; only dosage strength and uses are visible.[^17]
- Nepvol and Aerius omit contraindications, side effects, and storage conditions—requiring re-crawl or fallback to subcategory hints.[^15][^17]
- Constructed product_detail_link values require validation; they must be verified against live listings or discovered slugs.[^2]
- Subcategory overlaps with page-based products are likely; deduplication policies must be confirmed during production runs.[^2]
- Final deduplication and brand normalization rules need codification before serialization.
- Sequence mapping to strict sequential IDs (1…2280) requires confirmation during assembly; current rules are robust but must be validated.[^2]
- Cross-market pricing (EGP vs SAR) needs normalization and currency tagging; evidence provides anchors but not a universal standard.[^4][^5][^6][^8][^9][^10][^11]

